@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About · Sentinel Manufacturing Suite";
    // Optional if your _Layout supports it:
    ViewData["BodyClass"] = "about-page";
}

<main class="sentinel-main about-page">

    <!-- =========================
         HERO
    ========================== -->
    <section class="sentinel-section pb-5 pt-4 pt-lg-5">
        <div class="container-xl">
            <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
                <div class="col-lg-7">
                    <span class="sentinel-kicker">About Sentinel AI Systems</span>

                    <h1 class="display-5 fw-semibold mb-3">
                        Built by someone who has actually run factories — and now builds the systems behind them.
                    </h1>

                    <p class="lead text-secondary mb-3">
                        Sentinel Manufacturing Core Suite<span class="tm-mark">™</span> exists because too many plants are stuck between
                        paper, spreadsheets, and heavyweight systems that don’t match what happens on the floor.
                    </p>

                    <p class="text-secondary mb-0">
                        The goal is simple: give operators, technicians, and leaders one live picture of the plant — EM,
                        production, quality, safety, and parts — without a multi-year “digital transformation” project.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="col-lg-5">
                    <div class="sentinel-card p-4 h-100">
                        <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-2">
                            <span class="sentinel-pill">Our mission</span>
                            <span class="badge rounded-pill bg-primary bg-opacity-75">Practical AI</span>
                        </div>

                        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
                            Help manufacturing teams reduce downtime, standardize operations, and grow into full smart-factory
                            capability with tools that work on day one — not year three.
                        </p>

                        <ul class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                            <li>Put the right information in front of the right people mid-shift.</li>
                            <li>Bridge the gap between EM, production, quality, safety, and parts.</li>
                            <li>Make AI practical, safe, and grounded in real plant data.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mt-4 align-items-start">
                <div class="col-lg-7">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-2">Why Sentinel Manufacturing Core Suite<span class="tm-mark">™</span> exists</h2>
                    <p class="text-secondary mb-3">
                        If you walk a typical factory, you’ll see the same patterns: radios lighting up with EM calls,
                        downtime reasons scribbled on paper, spreadsheets trying to glue systems together, and leaders asking
                        for a simple view of “How are we actually running today?”
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-secondary mb-0">
                        Sentinel is designed as the operational layer between your people and the systems you already have
                        — CMMS, ERP, MES, historians — giving everyone a shared, live view of what’s happening right now.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="col-lg-5">
                    <div class="sentinel-card-soft p-4 h-100">
                        <div class="sentinel-card-badge mb-2">
                            Pain points we see in almost every plant
                        </div>
                        <ul class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                            <li>EM / breakdowns are tracked in radios and inboxes, not one queue.</li>
                            <li>Downtime coding is incomplete or inconsistent across lines.</li>
                            <li>Parts information is spread across ERP, spreadsheets, and memory.</li>
                            <li>Quality and safety events live in isolated logs, not tied to assets.</li>
                            <li>Leadership relies on backward-looking reports instead of live data.</li>
                            <li>AI feels abstract, risky, or bolted-on instead of practical.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========================
         PRINCIPLES (Sentinel cards, not bootstrap)
    ========================== -->
    <section class="sentinel-section pb-5">
        <div class="container-xl">
            <div class="sentinel-card p-4 p-md-5">
                <div class="row g-4">
                    <div class="col-lg-4">
                        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-2">How we build Sentinel</h2>
                        <p class="text-secondary mb-0">
                            Every feature is shaped by a few simple principles. They’re guardrails to keep the platform
                            practical for real plants — not just slide decks.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="col-lg-8">
                        <div class="row g-4">
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">Fast to deploy</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Start with a single line or area, prove value quickly, then scale.
                                        No nine-month implementation cycles required to see the first result.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">Operator-first</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Interfaces are designed for the people using them mid-shift: on mobile, with gloves,
                                        radios, and ten other things demanding attention.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">Plays well with others</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Sentinel doesn’t try to replace your CMMS, ERP, or MES. It connects and extends them,
                                        giving you one operational view.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">AI, but practical</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Recommendations and Q&amp;A grounded in your plant’s data — not generic models detached
                                        from reality.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">Built for uptime</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Environment separation, audit logging, backups, and connectivity options are treated
                                        as first-class features — not afterthoughts.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="about-principle">
                                    <div class="about-principle-title">Transparent and opinionated</div>
                                    <div class="about-principle-text">
                                        Sentinel brings a point of view on running EM, downtime, and operations — with configuration
                                        options to match your plant’s reality.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="mt-4">
                            <span class="sentinel-pill-stat">
                                <span class="fw-semibold">North star:</span>
                                reduce downtime and remove guesswork mid-shift
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========================
         ROADMAP CTA
    ========================== -->
    <section class="sentinel-section pb-5">
        <div class="container-xl">
            <div class="sentinel-card-soft p-4 p-md-5 d-flex flex-column flex-lg-row gap-3 align-items-start align-items-lg-center justify-content-between">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mb-2">Where Sentinel is headed</h2>
                    <p class="text-secondary mb-0">
                        Start with Factory Core foundations (EM + visibility), then grow into deeper ops intelligence,
                        multi-site rollups, and predictive layers as your roadmap matures.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Pricing" class="btn-sentinel-primary">
                        Explore tiers &amp; pricing
                    </a>
                    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact" asp-route-topic="site-conversation" class="btn-sentinel-ghost">
                        Talk about your site
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>